{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790964839,"nonce":"576qZe2K8EsPcBq0bt0bWBoAx6k=","title":"Interpreter: a method called through a Dynamic closure returns its primitive result unboxed","message":"Found while fixing 0a11f3d. In interp and hybrid, a bound method called through a Dynamic value stores its primitive result in the Dynamic register as it is, unboxed: Int reads as null, Float and Single crash hlp_value_to_string (SIGSEGV at the NaN-box tag). Present on the installed build of 2026-09-28 as well. jit was right.\n\n    class M { public function new() {} public function int():Int return 7; public function float():Float return 200.5; }\n    var m = new M();\n    var i:Dynamic = m.int;   trace(i());   // null, expected 7\n    var f:Dynamic = m.float; trace(f());   // crash, expected 200.5\n\nBoth interpreter dispatchers (the opcode loop and the SSA walker) stored a call's result by coercing it to the destination register's kind, which unboxes but never boxes. HashLink's dynamic call boxes a primitive result by the callee's return type.\n\nAlso in the same family, fixed with it:\n- Reflect.callMethod on a Single method read 0: the interpreter boxed an f32 from its f64 bits (box_value_as_dynamic_with_type), and hlp_make_dyn reads 4 bytes.\n- In every mode, a Single argument or result through hlp_call_method / ash_static_call was lost: the f32 slot was written as an f64, and the native trampolines passed and read f32 as a converted f64 rather than as the low bits of the float register.\n\nTest: crates/ash_cli/tests/generic_interface_bridge.rs, section `dynamic`, checked against stock HashLink 1.15 on the NUC.","files":null}]}